{
 "_comment": "McDonnell Douglas MD-82: FDM property values set after load and on every Fly!: the 'after start' panel state of the FlightGear MD-80 (Nasal acconfig PANEL.afterStart + the systems' init defaults), so the aircraft starts with engines running, generators on line, pumps on, bleeds open, IRS aligned. docs/MD80_FLIGHTGEAR_PORT.md Every FlightGear-side property the systems reference is listed (a JSBSim function throws at run time when a referenced property does not exist), hand-set values first, the rest at defaults. '_pulse' holds a property at 1 for N seconds of FDM time after every (re)start: FlightGear's acconfig keeps /systems/acconfig/autoconfig-running on for 5 s after setting the panel, and the systems shortcut on it (instant AHRS/IRS alignment, gauges to their place). '_links' are FlightGear property rules (core-rules.xml) copied src -> dst each step: the ignition / APU systems' starter and cutoff into the engine controls, which reach the JSBSim engines. _links values may be {src, factor, offset}: the IVSI reads it-autoflight/internal/vert-speed-fpm, which the Nasal autoflight filled from h-dot (x 60 here).",
 "_pulse": {
  "/systems/acconfig/autoconfig-running": 5.0
 },
 "_links": {
  "/controls/engines/engine[0]/cutoff": "/systems/ignition/cutoff-1",
  "/controls/engines/engine[1]/cutoff": "/systems/ignition/cutoff-2",
  "/controls/engines/engine[2]/cutoff": "/systems/apu/cutoff",
  "/controls/engines/engine[0]/starter": "/systems/ignition/starter-jsb-1",
  "/controls/engines/engine[1]/starter": "/systems/ignition/starter-jsb-2",
  "/controls/engines/engine[2]/starter": "/systems/apu/starter",
  "/it-autoflight/internal/vert-speed-fpm": {
   "src": "velocities/h-dot-fps",
   "factor": 60
  }
